{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5e7458847e466486","name":"GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat","source":{"id":"source:reference-5e7458847e466486","title":"GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat","revision":24583,"timestamp":"2024-11-04T00:17:23Z","sha256":"f3410db65c22e457b22378d10569c1c4da1ecb7f6610bcf29739cbb54674140f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24583","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=GAT-12h%20Skipray%20Blastboat&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5e7458847e466486","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dawn of Defiance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Defiance"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Jaws of the Sarlacc"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jaws_of_the_Sarlacc","referenceId":"reference:19132eb50b0196f2"},")"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Zann Consortium"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Zann_Consortium","referenceId":"reference:939c32df8a6e4fbd"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["This narrow ship seems to be little more than an oversized ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},". However, the weapons it carries- easily visible even from a distance- indicate that it is designed to take on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"}," and even small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},"."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sienar Fleet Systems GAT-12h, commonly referred to by the nickname \"Skipray,\" was released into service just prior to the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},". It was distinguished from the start as the smallest Imperial vessel (except for a handful of TIE prototypes) to be equipped with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," engines. The original design was intended to be used as an unescorted system patrol craft, capable of fending off ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and small ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though the naval units that used the \"Skipray\" raved about the vessel's awesome performance, it never quite caught on with Imperial High Command. Despite its capabilities, the ship was never accepted, and became another victim of the volatile policies that often controlled Imperial Naval doctrine. As a result, a large number of GAT-12h Skiprays wound up in service to planetary militias, corporate navies, mercenaries, pirates, and smugglers- especially, those of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Zann Consortium"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Zann_Consortium","referenceId":"reference:939c32df8a6e4fbd"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Skipray Blastboat was intended to fill the void between smaller snubfighters and larger capital-scale ships. In this regard, the Skipray was a complete success. Although a few Imperial fleet elements were equipped with Skiprays, the bulk of the ships were assigned to planetary defense forces or space stations. When possible, the GAT-12h is deployed in conjunction with ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," or teamed with one or more other Blastboats. When working in tandem, Skiprays team up to disable larger enemy ships before peeling off to deal with the incidental threat posed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and/or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat was intended to fill the void between smaller \"snub\" fighters and larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". In this regard, the Skipray was a complete success. Though a few Imperial Fleet elements were equipped with Skiprays, the bulk of the ships were assigned to planetary defense forces or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"},". When possible, the GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat is deployed in conjunction with ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"},", or is teamed up with one or more Skiprays. When working in tandem, Skiprays team up to disable larger enemy ships before peeling off to deal with the incidental threat posed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and/or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transports"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transports","referenceId":"reference:082a04e1f80578b3"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Given its capabilities, it is somewhat surprising that the GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat hosts a crew of only four: a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},", a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"},"/",{"tag":"a","children":["System Operator"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/System_Operator","referenceId":"reference:75f56e8f22b64ca4"},", and two ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunners"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunners"},". One ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," controls the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", while the other operates its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Ion Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Ion_Cannons"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Concussion Missiles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Concussion_Missiles"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Proton Torpedoes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Proton_Torpedoes"},". Though it is somewhat sluggish in space, the GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat is incredibly maneuverable when employed as an atmospheric craft. In an atmosphere, the Skipray gains a +2 bonus to its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," score.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["GAT-12h Skipray Blastboat Statistics (CL 15)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal* ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://sws